# The reverse proxy (docs/deployment.md, §13).
#
# Caddy terminates TLS with certificates it obtains itself, one per host, and
# forwards each host to its application. Two properties of the configuration
# are load-bearing and worth knowing before changing it:
#
#  - `reverse_proxy` passes the public `Host` header through unchanged. Every
#    application refuses a mutating request whose `Origin` does not match its
#    own `Host`, so a proxy that rewrote the header to the upstream's name
#    would make every form fail with what looks like a CORS error (§13).
#  - `X-Forwarded-For` is set by Caddy and read by the applications only as a
#    throttle key, never as an identity. The applications are reachable only
#    through this proxy on the compose network, so the header cannot be forged
#    from outside.
#
# The five hosts come from the environment (deploy/.env.production).

{$DOCTOR_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy doctor:3000
	encode gzip
}

{$ADMIN_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy admin:3000
	encode gzip
}

{$CENTRE_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy centre:3000
	encode gzip
}

{$VOLUNTEER_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy volunteer:3000
	encode gzip
}

{$DONOR_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy donor:3000
	encode gzip
}
